<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.15" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S3.F2.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The overview of HFM.
(a) <span id="S3.F2.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Constructing Centripetal Hyperbolic Space</span>: Establish a centripetal cross-modal hierarchy, optimizing textual roots near the origin and visual leaves toward the boundary.
(b) <span id="S3.F2.16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Learning Path-Decoupled Flows</span>: Tangent velocity fields <math id="S3.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℱ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> are optimized to guide features along isolated geodesic corridors. The step-wise consistency enforces trajectory decoupling in hyperbolic space.
(c) <span id="S3.F2.16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inference with Diameter-based Stopping</span>: The flow terminates at <math id="S3.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> once the distance to text prototypes drops below a dynamic threshold scaled by semantic diameter <math id="S3.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{txt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">txt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{txt}}</annotation></semantics></math> to alleviate over-transportation into the crowded
origin.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In this section, we present HFM, a path-decoupled framework designed to alleviate the path entanglement in few-shot adaptation. As illustrated in Figure </span><a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Path-Decoupled Hyperbolic Flow Matching for Few-Shot Adaptation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, our HFM comprises three phases:
1) </span><span id="S3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Constructing Centripetal Hyperbolic Space</span><span id="S3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (§</span><a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Constructing Centripetal Hyperbolic Space ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Path-Decoupled Hyperbolic Flow Matching for Few-Shot Adaptation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a><span id="S3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">): Establishing a centripetal hierarchy by anchoring textual roots at the origin and visual leaves at the boundary.
2) </span><span id="S3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Learning Path-Decoupled Flows</span><span id="S3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (§</span><a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Learning Path-Decoupled Flows ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Path-Decoupled Hyperbolic Flow Matching for Few-Shot Adaptation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a><span id="S3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">): Optimizing a tangent velocity field to confine transport within isolated geodesic corridors via step-wise and contrastive supervision. 3) </span><span id="S3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Inference with Diameter-based Stopping</span><span id="S3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (§</span><a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Inference with Diameter-based Stopping ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Path-Decoupled Hyperbolic Flow Matching for Few-Shot Adaptation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a><span id="S3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">): Employing a density-aware termination criterion to prevent over-transportation in crowded text region.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Preliminaries: Lorentz Model</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We first briefly introduce the key concepts of hyperbolic geometry on which our HFM relies. Following </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Desai et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pal et al., 2025</a><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we adopt the Lorentz model of hyperbolic space </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{L}^{n,\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{L}^{n,\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with </span><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">learnable</span><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> constant negative curvature </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\kappa</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (</span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">). In this model, each point </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}\in\mathbb{L}^{n,\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}\in\mathbb{L}^{n,\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> consists of a time-like scalar </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and a space-like vector </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, constrained by the geometric property </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle\bm{x},\bm{x}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}=-1/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\bm{x},\bm{x}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}=-1/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The Lorentzian inner product is formulated as
</span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\bm{x},\bm{y}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}=-x_{0}y_{0}+\langle\tilde{\bm{x}},\tilde{\bm{y}}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\bm{x},\bm{y}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}=-x_{0}y_{0}+\langle\tilde{\bm{x}},\tilde{\bm{y}}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the Euclidean inner product.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Geodesics.</span><span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The shortest path between two points on the manifold, written as </span><math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\kappa}}\text{arcosh}(-\kappa\langle\bm{x},\bm{y}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arcosh</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\kappa}}\text{arcosh}(-\kappa\langle\bm{x},\bm{y}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Tangent and Manifold Projection.</span><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
To map Euclidean features from CLIP into </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{L}^{n,\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{L}^{n,\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we employ the </span><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">exponential map</span><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nickel and Kiela, 2018</a><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> defined at the tangent space of a reference point </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
To align with this geometry, the original Euclidean feature </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is lifted into the </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-dimensional ambient tangent space </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\bm{z}}\mathbb{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\bm{z}}\mathbb{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, satisfying the orthogonality constraint with </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Consequently, the projection onto the manifold to obtain </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}\in\mathbb{L}^{n,\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}\in\mathbb{L}^{n,\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is formulated as:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!\bm{x}\!=\!\exp_{\bm{z}}^{\kappa}(\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\!)\!=\!\!\cosh(\sqrt{\kappa}\|\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\|_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})\bm{z}\!+\!\!\frac{\sinh(\sqrt{\kappa}\|\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\|_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})}{\sqrt{\kappa}\|\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\|_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}}\!\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo></mpadded><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">cosh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.660em;" width="0.660em"><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.052em" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo></mpadded><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">sinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!\bm{x}\!=\!\exp_{\bm{z}}^{\kappa}(\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\!)\!=\!\!\cosh(\sqrt{\kappa}\|\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\|_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})\bm{z}\!+\!\!\frac{\sinh(\sqrt{\kappa}\|\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\|_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})}{\sqrt{\kappa}\|\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}\|_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}}\!\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> refers to the lifted ambient vector derived from </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Conversely, the </span><span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">logarithmic map</span><span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> serves as the inverse operation, projecting a point </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> from the manifold back to the tangent space at </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to recover the Euclidean features:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}=\log_{\bm{z}}^{\kappa}(\bm{x})=\frac{\text{arccosh}(-\kappa\langle\bm{z},\bm{x}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})}{\sqrt{\langle\bm{z},\bm{x}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}^{2}-1/\kappa^{2}}}\Pi_{T_{\bm{z}}\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝔼</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arccosh</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{E}}=\log_{\bm{z}}^{\kappa}(\bm{x})=\frac{\text{arccosh}(-\kappa\langle\bm{z},\bm{x}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})}{\sqrt{\langle\bm{z},\bm{x}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}^{2}-1/\kappa^{2}}}\Pi_{T_{\bm{z}}\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S3.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{T_{\bm{z}}\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x})=\bm{x}+\kappa\langle\bm{z},\bm{x}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{T_{\bm{z}}\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x})=\bm{x}+\kappa\langle\bm{z},\bm{x}\rangle_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p3.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denotes the orthogonal projection onto the tangent space.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Constructing Centripetal Hyperbolic Space</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To address disordered cross-modality flows, we first align the latent geometry into a </span><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">centripetal hierarchy</span><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (Figure </span><a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Path-Decoupled Hyperbolic Flow Matching for Few-Shot Adaptation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">a). Formally, let </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denote the hyperbolic textual prototypes (serving as semantic roots/targets) and </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denote the hyperbolic visual features (serving as entailment leaves/sources). This alignment resolves path entanglement by transforming arbitrary transport paths into ordered centripetal flows from </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The exponential boundary expansion guarantees sufficient initialization spacing for visual feature </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, reducing spatial trajectory overlap during inward transport.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Geometric Stratification.</span><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> We explicitly impose a centripetal hierarchy by initializing learnable scalars as: </span><math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\text{txt}}&lt;\alpha_{\text{img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">txt</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">img</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\text{txt}}&lt;\alpha_{\text{img}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to modulate the feature norm before tangent to manifold projection. This configuration anchors text near the origin and pushes images to the boundary (§Figure </span><a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Path-Decoupled Hyperbolic Flow Matching for Few-Shot Adaptation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">a), creating an explicit geometric prior for inward transport.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Centripetal hyperbolic alignment.</span><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
To solidify this hierarchy, we optimize the embeddings using joint objectives that enforce both geometric entailment and semantic discrimination.
In Figure </span><a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Path-Decoupled Hyperbolic Flow Matching for Few-Shot Adaptation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">a, we employ the </span><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">hyperbolic entailment loss</span><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Desai et al., 2023</a><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to enforce a partial order where the text prototype </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (parent) spatially entails the image feature </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (child).
Formally, we constrain </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to lie within the entailment cone of </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by minimizing the angular violation:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{entail}}=\max\left(0,\pi-\angle\bm{0}\bm{x}_{1}\bm{x}_{0}-\omega(\bm{x}_{1})\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">entail</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟎</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{entail}}=\max\left(0,\pi-\angle\bm{0}\bm{x}_{1}\bm{x}_{0}-\omega(\bm{x}_{1})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where the term </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi-\angle\bm{0}\bm{x}_{1}\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟎</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi-\angle\bm{0}\bm{x}_{1}\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> corresponds to the exterior angle at </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, explicitly quantifying the deviation of the child </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> from the parent’s radial axis.
The term </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega(\bm{x}_{1})=\arcsin(2H/\|\bm{x}_{1}\|_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arcsin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega(\bm{x}_{1})=\arcsin(2H/\|\bm{x}_{1}\|_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the cone aperture, which naturally narrows as the prototype’s radius increases.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Complementing this, we use a hyperbolic contrastive loss </span><math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">con</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to enforce semantic discrimination. It minimizes the geodesic distance between the image feature </span><math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and its ground-truth text prototype </span><math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{c}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{c}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, while maximizing distances to other prototypes in the support set:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}=-\log\frac{\exp\left(-d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x}_{0},\bm{x}^{c}_{1})/\tau\right)}{\sum_{k}\exp\left(-d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x}_{0},\bm{x}^{k}_{1})/\tau\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">con</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}=-\log\frac{\exp\left(-d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x}_{0},\bm{x}^{c}_{1})/\tau\right)}{\sum_{k}\exp\left(-d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\bm{x}_{0},\bm{x}^{k}_{1})/\tau\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Learning Path-Decoupled Flows</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Having aligned the centripetal hierarchy, we proceed to learn the transport dynamics that guide entailment from visual leaves to semantic roots.
Unlike standard Riemannian flow matching </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen and Lipman, 2022</a><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> that typically requires integrating an ordinary differential equation (ODE) over a continuous velocity field, we propose path-decoupled HFM.
Our core insight is to exploit </span><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">step-wise transport</span><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024</a><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to enable explicit geometric supervision (§Figure </span><a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Path-Decoupled Hyperbolic Flow Matching for Few-Shot Adaptation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">b).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Geodesic Path.</span><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
Similar to the plain Euclidean flow matching </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2025</a><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we define the ground-truth trajectory as the geodesic path on </span><math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> connecting the source image </span><math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> explicitly to its ground-truth class prototype </span><math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. This strict pairing disentangles the optimization into independent source-target tasks, effectively eliminating inter-class interference </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2025</a><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Tangent Velocity Alignment.</span><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
To learn the transport dynamics, we sample paired states </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{x}_{t},\bm{x}_{t+\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{x}_{t},\bm{x}_{t+\delta})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> from the ground-truth geodesic path. Specifically, given a random time </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and a step size </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we aim to predict the update that transports the feature from </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t+\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t+\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Our network </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℱ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> predicts an ambient vector at state </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, which is explicitly projected onto the local tangent space to ensure geometric validity:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}_{t}=\Pi_{T_{\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{L}}\left(\mathcal{F}_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℱ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}_{t}=\Pi_{T_{\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{L}}\left(\mathcal{F}_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{T_{\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{T_{\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{L}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denotes the orthogonal projection onto the tangent space at </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
We then model the discrete evolution by mapping this tangent velocity back onto the manifold via the exponential map </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen and Lipman, 2022</a><span id="S3.SS3.p3.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS3.p3.2.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}=\exp_{\bm{x}_{t}}^{\kappa}(\delta\cdot\bm{v}_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}=\exp_{\bm{x}_{t}}^{\kappa}(\delta\cdot\bm{v}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This parameterization ensures that the predicted next state </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> strictly resides on the hyperbolic manifold </span><math id="S3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p3.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Path-decoupled Objective.</span><span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
We optimize the network using a path-decoupled objective that enforces both step-wise trajectory consistency and semantic separation. Crucially, both losses operate on the predicted future state </span><math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, enabling direct rectification of the flow.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1) Step-wise Consistency Loss:</span><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
To ensure the learned flow precisely follows the geodesic path, we minimize the squared Riemannian distance between the predicted state </span><math id="S3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and the ground-truth target </span><math id="S3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t+\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t+\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{step}}=\|d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta},\bm{x}_{t+\delta})\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">step</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{step}}=\|d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta},\bm{x}_{t+\delta})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2) Inter-Class Decoupling Loss:</span><span id="S3.SS3.p5.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
To prevent the flow from drifting into the attraction basins of incorrect classes, we impose a “semantic guardrail” via a dynamic hyperbolic contrastive loss. Unlike the static alignment, this objective forces the predicted intermediate state </span><math id="S3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p5.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to maximize its similarity with the corresponding prototype </span><math id="S3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p5.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> while repelling all negative prototypes:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{icd}}=-\log\frac{\exp\left(-d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta},\bm{x}_{1}^{c})/\tau\right)}{\sum_{k}\exp\left(-d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta},\bm{x}_{1}^{k})/\tau\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">icd</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{icd}}=-\log\frac{\exp\left(-d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta},\bm{x}_{1}^{c})/\tau\right)}{\sum_{k}\exp\left(-d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta},\bm{x}_{1}^{k})/\tau\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The total objective is </span><math id="S3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{step}}+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{\text{icd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">step</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">icd</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{step}}+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{\text{icd}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p5.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The overall training procedure is summarized in Algorithm </span><a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 Learning Path-Decoupled Flows ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Path-Decoupled Hyperbolic Flow Matching for Few-Shot Adaptation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="S3.SS3.p5.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. By penalizing semantic deviations at each intermediate step, this mechanism strictly confines trajectories to class-specific corridors, thereby eliminating the path entanglement issue.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Training Path-Decoupled Flows</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Input:</span><span id="alg1.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> paired hyperbolic image features and text features </span><math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(\bm{x}_{0},\bm{x}_{1})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(\bm{x}_{0},\bm{x}_{1})\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, stepsize </span><math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, weight </span><math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Initialize:</span><span id="alg1.l2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> flow network parameters </span><math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">repeat</span><span id="alg1.l3.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">

</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{x}_{0},\bm{x}_{1})\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{x}_{0},\bm{x}_{1})\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l4.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}\leftarrow\exp_{\bm{x}_{0}}^{\kappa}(t\cdot\log_{\bm{x}_{0}}^{\kappa}(\bm{x}_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}\leftarrow\exp_{\bm{x}_{0}}^{\kappa}(t\cdot\log_{\bm{x}_{0}}^{\kappa}(\bm{x}_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t+\delta}\leftarrow\exp_{\bm{x}_{0}}^{\kappa}((t+\delta)\cdot\log_{\bm{x}_{0}}^{\kappa}(\bm{x}_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t+\delta}\leftarrow\exp_{\bm{x}_{0}}^{\kappa}((t+\delta)\cdot\log_{\bm{x}_{0}}^{\kappa}(\bm{x}_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}_{t}\leftarrow\Pi_{T_{\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{L}}(\mathcal{F}_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝕃</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℱ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}_{t}\leftarrow\Pi_{T_{\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{L}}(\mathcal{F}_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}\leftarrow\exp_{\bm{x}_{t}}^{\kappa}(\delta\cdot\bm{v}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta}\leftarrow\exp_{\bm{x}_{t}}^{\kappa}(\delta\cdot\bm{v}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\|d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta},\bm{x}_{t+\delta})\|^{2}+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{\text{icd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.710em">𝕃</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">icd</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\|d_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathbb{L}}(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t+\delta},\bm{x}_{t+\delta})\|^{2}+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{\text{icd}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  Update </span><math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> using gradient descent to minimize </span><math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l10.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
